hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  gonna answer question from Fatima who's  one of my facebook readers who wrote in  about how to start a new business that  doesn't require money so specifically  the question was I'm a third year  student in accounting and you want to be  an entrepreneur after I finished my  course my question is what business  should I do especially since I don't  have capital right now  Thank You Fatima so thanks for the  question I think it's a great question  one that a lot of people are thinking  about how do I start a business not a  lot of money the key here is you don't  need a lot of money to start almost any  business there are very few businesses  where you absolutely need to have a ton  of money to get started and so what I  would encourage you to do is instead of  trying to find an opportunity where you  don't need a lot of money look at  something where you feel that you can  add a lot of value to and that you're  really passionate about that's gonna be  the key you look at any famous  entrepreneur how they got started and  you ask them what the key to success was  almost always one of the key reasons to  come back is that they had a strong  passion for that business it wasn't just  to make money they wanted to change the  way things were done in a certain  industry you wanted to add a lot of  value to people's lives so don't just go  out looking for the opportunity to make  money you'll often find that the the  people who just try to make money really  do and it's because they quit at the  first sign of trouble they don't put in  the hard work to get past the hurdles I  come in front of them and it's only  because you love your business so much  and you love what you're doing and you  look how much you're helping people  that's what gives you the fuel to keep  going even when times get tough a lot of  entrepreneurs say that they would do  what they were doing for their business  even if they weren't making any money  because of how good it makes them feel  but the value that you they're adding  and they would go and get a job to  support this passion are there so that's  what you want to try to find you want to  find what you love so much that you're  really helping other people and you  would do even if you're not getting paid  to do it because you really love what  you're doing for me I love helping  entrepreneurs I love making these videos  I love  talking entrepreneurs I do a lot of this  stuff without getting paid I'm making  this video for you because I'm not I'm  not getting paid to do it unless there's  some secret person paying me that I'm  not quite sure about but really I don't  make a lot I don't make money from from  these videos but I do it because I love  doing it I love helping entrepreneurs  hopefully you can take this advice go  away put it into your business and  become successful so that's what you  want to find with your own  entrepreneurship venture something that  you're really passionate about will you  wake up excited to do it and you're you  know you're adding a lot of value to  people's lives and that's gonna be the  key is helping other people from there  if you're looking at ways to not spend a  lot of money and that's he you find a  lot of the successful companies started  just from bootstrapping  start a service so service companies are  easier to startup they don't fail as  often as product companies and retail  companies the idea here is you not  spending a lot of money to get started  but you're spending a lot of sweat  equity to put in your time in to see if  it'll work the challenge that people  face on the product side is you spend a  lot of time creating this product you  spend a lot of money buying this product  making purchases and you have a huge  inventory and then doesn't sell and  you've invested all this money into this  product that then sitting in your  basement or your you know extra room or  whatever it is and you can't sell it and  so you're out of pack you have to go  back and get another job or if you're  doing a service it brings you closer to  your customer you really understand what  their pain points are and how you can  help them and then you're not spending a  lot of money you don't really need to  spend any money to start a service-based  business you know you can protection of  a business card maybe a website if you  want but you don't need to spend money  it's more your time as you're able to  build it up and you work with a couple  clients and you know you might be tired  of treating your time for money then you  can't expand into a product type of  business but you have some cash flow  built in from your service so definitely  look at whatever field you're really  passionate about you feel like you got a  lot of value to your clients start a  service around that the third key point  that I want to leave you with is try not  to spend money until you're making money  anybody can spend money it's easy to  spend money if I give you a million  dollars you can go and spend it a  million different ways I'm sure you  could and this is a challenge I had when  I was in the venture capital business we  saw so many entrepreneurs come to us  looking to spend money what you want to  be is that entrepreneur who can earn the  money and so try not to go out and make  a lot of purchases and spend any money  on your business until you're making  something back and this is something  I've tried to apply to all of my new  ideas with my company every new thing  that we try out I'll spend some time and  energy putting it into a see if it'll  work but I won't spend any money on it  until I'm making some money from it  exactly just a couple times with these  videos it's a good example because  you're watching this video so it's a  good medium when I first started doing  video I really wanted to get in a video  because I found that was really a visual  learner and I learned a lot more from  video than just hearing something or  reading something so I wanted to get in  the video but I didn't have a revenue  model behind it so I didn't want to go  and spend money on you know camera  lighting tripod all the things that you  need to make video work I didn't want to  spend money on it because I didn't know  AI would commit to this and continue  doing this if I would like it or not you  don't know if you're gonna like a  project until you actually give in to it  and I didn't know if I'd ever be able to  make money from it so the quickest way  to do it is just start trying it out I  took my regular camera  and just started recording myself and  it's just some questions that people had  written into me and I really did like it  and if you go back to my YouTube channel  and look at the earlier videos they were  really bad the the the quality of the  content was pretty good but the lighting  was bad the camera was bad the audio is  bad because it didn't spend money on a  microphone so that's how we kind of  started off but I've continued with it I  realized I really enjoyed doing it and  eventually was able to find a way to  monetize the video is not all the videos  but some of them through corporate  sponsorships I know you know the money  from those ones help me create all the  other ones so I can spend the time I  want doing these types of videos even  though I'm not getting paid to do it  because it's fun but it gave me the  ability to go and buy a camera and buy  tripod  microphone get some lighting hire an  editor create an intro have some music  on it just to improve the experience and  make the videos that much better so it  all started from nothing like it could  have gone nowhere could have spent all  this money on this gear and I did two  videos and shut the whole project down  and now I'm stuck with all this extra  gear that I'm never gonna use again so  try not to spend money until you're  making money there's a kind of a long  story they kind of get back to that  point whatever business you're going  into if you're passionate about it and  you're creating it around the service  you don't need to spend money you can  find ways to be able to get some  contracts without spending money and  then even though they may not be big  contracts if you can prove to yourself  that hey I'm able to make a little bit  of money here and you really enjoy doing  this this is definitely what you want to  keep doing then you can invest some of  the money that you make back into the  things that will help you grow the  business bigger and bigger bigger and  continue expand from there so maybe that  helped  maybe not the specific answer you were  looking for people sometimes want to  kind of bullet shot here's the exact way  to go about and do it in the type of  business you want to run without any  money but the good news is you can do it  around anything and the more you can  build a business around your passion the  more money you're gonna make and the  more fun you're gonna have to and that's  part of it you're gonna put in a lot of  hours running a business you might as  well be doing something that you really  enjoy and that you know you're helping a  lot of people out instead of just trying  to make some money off of it so  hopefully that helped that if you guys  liked the video please give it a thumbs  up below it really makes you want to do  more these videos for you guys and if  you have a comment about this video or  if you have a question for your own  company feel free to leave it in the  comment section below I always read  those to try to respond to everybody as  much as I can so thank you  and I'll see you in the next episode  you
 

